# Dependency Setup

- Packages like `discord.js` and `@tavily/core` are listed in `dependencies` but aren't auto-installed.  
- These should probably be in `peerDependencies` instead if they're required.  
- Right now, users have to manually hunt these down when errors pop up.  

# Module Exports

The current `package.json` exports:

```json
{
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "import": {
        "@daydreamsai/core": "./src/index.ts",
        "types": "./src/index.ts",
        "default": "./src/index.ts"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This makes consumers deal with raw TypeScript files. Could we switch to:

```json
{
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "import": "./dist/index.js",
      "types": "./dist/index.d.ts"
    }
  }
}
```

This would work out-of-the-box with standard TS/Node setups. Am I misunderstanding the current approach?
